[LTO] Mark a symbol whose definition has a different IR name from an earlier reference

addModuleToGlobalRes already treats a symbol with two IR names as visible outside the summary, since ThinLTO gives the names two GUIDs and would otherwise drop the definition. It only noticed when the definition was read first. With a reference read before the definition the definition's name replaced the reference's, was compared with itself, and the definition was deleted as dead.

On a target with a global prefix a header that declares a function with an asm label gives the declaration the IR name \01___foo while the definition is __foo. Linking dxvk for i686 mingw hit this: libdisplay-info was read before the libmingwex member that defines __mingw_snprintf.


diff --git a/llvm/lib/LTO/LTO.cpp b/llvm/lib/LTO/LTO.cpp
index b591f9c6a831..2d85088ff042 100644
--- a/llvm/lib/LTO/LTO.cpp
+++ b/llvm/lib/LTO/LTO.cpp
@@ -735,10 +735,16 @@ void LTO::addModuleToGlobalRes(ArrayRef<InputFile::Symbol> Syms,
 
     auto &GlobalRes = (*GlobalResolutions)[SymbolName];
     GlobalRes.UnnamedAddr &= Sym.isUnnamedAddr();
+    // A reference read before the definition leaves its IR name in GlobalRes,
+    // and the definition replaces it below. The check on the names has to see
+    // that they differ in that order as much as in the other.
+    bool IRNameChanged = false;
     if (Res.Prevailing) {
       assert(!GlobalRes.Prevailing &&
              "Multiple prevailing defs are not allowed");
       GlobalRes.Prevailing = true;
+      IRNameChanged =
+          !GlobalRes.IRName.empty() && GlobalRes.IRName != Sym.getIRName();
       GlobalRes.IRName = std::string(Sym.getIRName());
     } else if (!GlobalRes.Prevailing && GlobalRes.IRName.empty()) {
       // Sometimes it can be two copies of symbol in a module and prevailing
@@ -762,7 +768,7 @@ void LTO::addModuleToGlobalRes(ArrayRef<InputFile::Symbol> Syms,
     // based on mangled name, but this requires an access to the Target Triple
     // and would be relatively invasive on the codebase.
     // FIXME: use the GUID member of GlobalRes.
-    if (GlobalRes.IRName != Sym.getIRName()) {
+    if (IRNameChanged || GlobalRes.IRName != Sym.getIRName()) {
       GlobalRes.Partition = GlobalResolution::External;
       GlobalRes.VisibleOutsideSummary = true;
     }
